        <icon:inputDescription>Grinding feed and media: Organic/inorganic samples; grinding bowls and balls selected for feed material; states: Dry grinding or wet grinding; media/compatibility are configuration-dependent; phase: Dry solid, emulsion or suspension as specified&#10;Mains input: 100–240 V ±10%; approx. 10 A at 115 V or 5 A at 230 V; maximum power approximately 1100 W; states: Mains off/on; voltage-change procedure and restart protection apply&#10;Program parameters: Speed up to 1100 rpm; time up to 999 min; pause up to 99 min; cycles up to 99; states: Numeric program entries; starts only after bowl/closing checks&#10;Cover and bowl sensing: Sensors check grinding bowls and cover mechanism; states: Bowl detected/not detected; stationary-drive/cover conditions; safety checks before starting&#10;Additional documented controls/states: lid opening/locking control.&#10;Source: Manuals/FRITSCH PULVERISETTE 7 premium line__linked-manual__34deccc603.pdf, PDF p. 18.</icon:inputDescription>
        <icon:inputOutputStatus>catalog_io_row</icon:inputOutputStatus>
        <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>A; V; W; cycle count; mL; min; mm; rpm; state; µm</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
        <icon:outputDescription>Ground sample: Manual reports dry d50 &lt;20 µm and wet d50 &lt;0.1 µm depending on material; states: Ground material; actual size requires measurement and depends on process; phase: Dry powder or wet suspension&#10;Operating/fault indication: Display signals overload; drive stops for overheating, blockage or excessive imbalance; states: Grinding; paused/stopped; reduced-speed overload; thermal/blockage/imbalance shutdown; no automatic restart after power loss</icon:outputDescription>
        <icon:reportedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/A"/>
