  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment/REQ-EQ-027">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentModel"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/ProductModel"/>
    <dct:identifier>REQ-EQ-027</dct:identifier>
    <schema:name>Gamry corrosion cell</schema:name>
    <schema:manufacturer rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/manufacturer/gamry"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment.csv#row=616"/>
    <dct:isPartOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/dataset/equipment"/>
    <icon:identity>
      <icon:IdentityProfile rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment/REQ-EQ-027/identity">
        <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment.csv#row=616"/>
        <icon:inCategory rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M57"/>
        <icon:recordKind>component_family</icon:recordKind>
      </icon:IdentityProfile>
    </icon:identity>
    <icon:inputOutputProfile>
      <icon:InputOutputProfile rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-027">
        <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv#row=612"/>
        <dct:source rdf:resource="https://www.gamry.com/assets/Uploads/MultiPort-Manual-Rev1-4.pdf"/>
        <icon:importedDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
        <icon:inputDescription>The linked source is the MultiPort cell kit: electrolyte, a metal working-electrode specimen, graphite counter electrode and a separately selected reference electrode. Optional purge/blanket gas requires a vent; the cell is not a pressure vessel. Optional jacket accepts circulating bath fluid; spare ports accept a thermometer/pH probe or reactant addition. Electrode leads connect to a separate potentiostat. Gas modes are purge, blanket and vent; no electronic command-state map is provided for the passive cell.&#10;Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.</icon:inputDescription>
        <icon:inputOutputStatus>catalog_io_row</icon:inputOutputStatus>
        <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>mL (MultiPort standard operating volume: 1000 mL); cm² or in² (nominal gasket-covered electrode area); mm/in (specimen geometry). Voltage, current, impedance, temperature and pH units/ranges depend on separately installed measuring instruments.&#10;Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
        <icon:outputDescription>Electrode potential/current response is conveyed to the connected potentiostat; corrosion/impedance results depend on that instrument and method. The passive cell itself does not acquire or export digital measurements. Purge gas exits the vent; the reacted electrolyte/specimen remain in the cell. The unspecified inventory row does not confirm the MultiPort model or an eight-channel potentiostat.&#10;Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.</icon:outputDescription>
        <icon:reportedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliL"/>
        <icon:sourceRow>12</icon:sourceRow>
        <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
        <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
      </icon:InputOutputProfile>
    </icon:inputOutputProfile>
    <icon:associations>
      <icon:CatalogAssociations rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment/REQ-EQ-027/associations">
        <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment.csv#row=616"/>
        <icon:associationBasis>curated supplement; material/process links are proposed context, not verified model capability</icon:associationBasis>
