        <icon:modelStatus>facility_documented_model</icon:modelStatus>
        <icon:notes>FIB-SEM uses ion species such asAu/Ge/Si for direct milling, plus an FE-SEM column for process control. It is not electron-beam resist lithography M59. Existing M61 source class/subtypes currently cover reactive-ion/plasma and wet etching, so a dedicated FIB nanopatterning class/route would be needed before offering its ion-writing function. RAITH uppercase is the already-verified canonical manufacturer key; separate Raith row should not cause unverified display.  Exact-model official technical product page; an operator manual was not independently located. No verified current US machine purchase price. Facility usage rates are excluded. Optional characterization candidates do not change required process steps.</icon:notes>
        <icon:priceStatus>no_public_exact_msrp_confirmed</icon:priceStatus>
        <icon:reviewDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-17</icon:reviewDate>
      </icon:ReviewProfile>
    </icon:review>
