        <dct:source rdf:resource="https://www.oceanoptics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Flame-User-Manual.pdf"/>
        <icon:importedDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
        <icon:inputDescription>Optical input through the SMA fibre connector; acquisition integration time, averaging and trigger selection from the host PC over USB or serial connection. USB provides power. Normal/free-run, external synchronous, external hardware-level and external hardware-edge triggering are documented. DD4 pin 2 accepts the external TTL trigger (5 or 3.3 V as specified); GPIO pins are not 5 V tolerant. Exact Flame-S/Flame-T detector, slit and wavelength configuration is unspecified in this row.&#10;Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.</icon:inputDescription>
        <icon:inputOutputStatus>catalog_io_row</icon:inputOutputStatus>
        <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>nm (wavelength/resolution); µm (slit width); µs, ms and s (integration/trigger timing); Hz (scan rate); V and mA (electrical interface/power); detector counts and configured logic states (dimensionless). Detector-specific integration ranges must not be merged between Flame-S and Flame-T.&#10;Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
        <icon:outputDescription>Wavelength-resolved spectra and derived absorbance/reflectance/emission through the host software, subject to calibration. Red LED steady=powered; green LED steady=ready and flashing=acquiring. Single/continuous strobe, lamp-enable, configurable GPIO and serial transmit are documented at the DD4 interface. Pin voltages/directions vary; refer to the pin table rather than treating every signal as 5 V TTL.&#10;Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.</icon:outputDescription>
        <icon:reportedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HZ"/>
        <icon:reportedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM"/>
        <icon:reportedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoM"/>
        <icon:sourceRow>738</icon:sourceRow>
        <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
        <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
      </icon:InputOutputProfile>
    </icon:inputOutputProfile>
