    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=69"/>
    <skos:notation>M70</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Programmable thermocyclers</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-requested Opentrons module scope; official GEN1/GEN2 identities checked. Two model generations, not ten researched interchangeable market examples. No nanomaterial manufacturing relevance inferred from PCR/control documentation.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M71">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=70"/>
    <skos:notation>M71</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Laboratory drying and curing ovens</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Atmospheric-pressure natural/forced-convection laboratory ovens for drying, ageing and thermal curing. Excludes M18 vacuum ovens, tube furnaces and hydrothermal reactors. Actual solvent ventilation, atmosphere and material compatibility must be checked. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M72">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=71"/>
    <skos:notation>M72</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Laboratory compression and hot presses</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Laboratory uniaxial mechanical/hydraulic compression presses, with unheated or heated platens/dies for compaction, pellet making, lamination and hot compression. Excludes nanoimprint lithography M60 and SPS category M69. Heated operation is model/configuration dependent. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M73">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=77"/>
    <skos:notation>M73</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Ion implantation systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Complete systems that produce, select, accelerate and deliver an ion beam into a solid substrate for implantation or material modification. Excludes generic plasma etchers, ion-milling-only tools and ion-source components. Selection of catalyst species, dose, substrate and end station requires model-specific review. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M74">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=78"/>
    <skos:notation>M74</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Metal melting and casting systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Integrated metal melting/alloying and casting systems with suitable mould/crucible hardware, atmosphere control and casting arrangement; includes vacuum/inert induction and arc-melting systems with casting options. Distinct from annealing-only induction heaters. Alloy chemistry, reactivity, casting dimensions and optional hardware must be checked. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M75">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=79"/>
    <skos:notation>M75</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Metal extrusion presses</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Purpose-built presses that force a metal billet through a die to make elongated rods, wire, tubes or profiles. Excludes CNC machining, rolling mills, polymer-only screw extruders and generic presses without documented metal extrusion capability. Alloy, die, billet heater, extrusion ratio and force must be checked. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M76">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=73"/>
    <skos:notation>M76</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Aerosol dryer</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. In-line diffusion or membrane dryer that removes solvent vapor from an aerosol without intentionally collecting its particles. Distinct from spray dryers and compressed-air dryers. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M77">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=74"/>
    <skos:notation>M77</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Aerosol charge conditioner</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Aerosol neutralizer or charger that establishes a controlled particle-charge distribution before electrical-mobility classification. Bipolar and unipolar instruments require the matching measurement model. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M78">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=75"/>
    <skos:notation>M78</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Aerosol particle detector</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Condensation particle counter or aerosol electrometer used to detect/count particles or measure particle-borne charge after classification. Electrometers require a known charge state to infer particle count. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M79">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=76"/>
    <skos:notation>M79</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Aerosol collection system</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Impaction or electrostatic collection apparatus that captures aerosol particles onto substrates for recovery or offline analysis; selecting a collector requires the relevant size range, flow and collection substrate. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M80">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=80"/>
    <skos:notation>M80</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Laser-ablation reaction chambers</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. Reaction chambers/flow cells and their optical coupling for nanoparticle laser ablation in liquids. Laser source remains M56. Laboratory custom builds require configuration-specific engineering; analytical LA-ICP-MS cells are not assumed suitable. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M81">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=72"/>
    <skos:notation>M81</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Laboratory mortar and grinding mills</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized required process-slot extension. General laboratory nonplanetary grinding and mortar systems for dry/wet size reduction, powder mixing and sample preparation. Record mechanism explicitly: pressure/friction mortar grinders differ from cutting/impact batch mills. Excludes high-energy planetary mills in M12; category membership does not establish nano-size output. Market membership is functional classification; exact process/configuration suitability requires review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M82">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=81"/>
    <skos:notation>M82</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Liquid handling and pipetting systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Manual/electronic pipettes and dispensers, plus automated pipetting workstations; complements pumps M07 and general robots M62. Candidate for transfers and feed preparation; no pipette model is asserted by the source rows. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M83">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=82"/>
    <skos:notation>M83</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Magnetic particle separation systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Magnetic racks, separators and flow-through magnetic recovery assemblies. P33 step 4 is an optional characterization-preparation branch, not a universal production requirement. Representative magnetic-bead racks are not validated for the cited magnetite formulation. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M84">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=83"/>
    <skos:notation>M84</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Quench tanks and immersion cooling vessels</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Water/oil/polymer quench baths and tanks, kept distinct from furnaces and recirculating chillers. P35 explicitly records a water-quench vessel but no make/model; the cited manufacturer page establishes the equipment type only. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M85">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=84"/>
    <skos:notation>M85</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Wet-process benches and batch solvent-exchange stations</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Development, rinsing, lift-off, washing and batch solvent-exchange stations, with operation-specific configuration. A planning grouping; a wafer solvent bench does not automatically fit colloidal washing or gel solvent exchange. Separate subtypes and chemistry compatibility are required. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M86">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=85"/>
    <skos:notation>M86</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Process data acquisition and feedback-control systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Sensor interfaces, DAQ hardware and controllers; software and feedback policies remain configuration data. Existing optical instruments remain M35/M40 and pumps remain M07; DAQ type evidence does not establish a valid closed-loop controller for either cited process. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M87">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=86"/>
    <skos:notation>M87</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Casting/moulding fixtures and ambient drying stations</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Scaffold moulds, casting fixtures and controlled ambient conditioning enclosures. Proposal derived from the P16 source action. An accessory-level extension may fit better than an M-class; do not substitute a heated oven for room-temperature drying. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M88">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=87"/>
    <skos:notation>M88</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Powder dispensing and die-loading systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>User-authorized implementation, 2026-10-17. Metered powder feeders/dispensers and configurable die-filling/loading assemblies. Candidate for a future automated P41 loading branch. Commercial powder dosing establishes the equipment type, not graphite-die or nanocarbon compatibility. Market alternatives are not source-paper apparatus or validated process configurations.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M89">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=88"/>
    <skos:notation>M89</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Two-photon lithography and micro/nano printing systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Two-photon/multiphoton polymerization and grayscale direct laser writing; excludes UV mask aligners and electron-beam writers. Alternative two-photon photopolymer branch in P06, not a drop-in replacement for the electron-beam/metal recipe. Compatible resist, development and geometry must be chosen; no automatic metal etch/transfer requirement.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M90">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=89"/>
    <skos:notation>M90</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Cryogenic grid vitrification systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Grid plunge/jet/blotless vitrification for cryo-TEM of hydrated dispersions; excludes bulk high-pressure freezers and freeze dryers. Optional grid vitrification before TEM verification of hydrated dispersions. Selecting this class requires a cryo-TEM configuration in the M39 verification slot. Not bulk freezing or freeze drying.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M91">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=90"/>
    <skos:notation>M91</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Magnetic-property measurement systems (SQUID/VSM)</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Complete SQUID and VSM magnetic-property systems, including configured PPMS+VSM; not particle separation magnets or Hall-only gaussmeters. Optional magnetic-moment/hysteresis verification of magnetite; not magnetic separation or a synthesis operation.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M92">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=91"/>
    <skos:notation>M92</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>ICP-OES elemental analysis</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Inductively coupled plasma optical emission spectroscopy for elemental analysis of prepared/digested samples. Not ICP-MS or UV-visible absorption. Optional elemental composition/concentration after suitable digestion, dilution and calibration. Not particle-size or phase measurement.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M93">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=92"/>
    <skos:notation>M93</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Contact stylus profilometry</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Mechanical stylus surface height, film thickness and roughness measurement; distinct from optical profilometry and AFM. Optional contact profilometry of accessible films/steps; stylus force, film damage, roughness and substrate suitability require review. Not AFM or optical profilometry.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M94">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=93"/>
    <skos:notation>M94</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Nanoindentation and nanomechanical testing</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Instrumented nanoindentation/nanoscratch platforms for nanoscale mechanical response; equipment configuration and sample preparation determine suitability. Optional mechanical response of suitably prepared nanostructured bulk/composite surfaces; indentation depth, substrate and polishing effects require review.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M95">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=94"/>
    <skos:notation>M95</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS)</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Surface elemental and chemical-state analysis using XPS/ESCA; not powder X-ray diffraction. Optional surface elemental/chemical-state analysis; vacuum compatibility and transfer/contamination are sample-specific. Not bulk composition or XRD.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M96">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=95"/>
    <skos:notation>M96</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Auger electron spectroscopy systems</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Surface elemental/chemical-state analysis by Auger electron spectroscopy. Not XPS or SEM-EDS. Vacuum, sample and beam-damage constraints remain model-specific. Optional local surface elemental mapping for vacuum-compatible specimens; charging and beam damage must be checked. Not XPS or SEM-EDS.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M97">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=96"/>
    <skos:notation>M97</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>Quartz crystal microbalance with dissipation monitoring</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>QCM instruments that measure dissipation in addition to frequency. Includes ring-down QCM-D and explicitly labelled bandwidth/impedance-derived dissipation; measurement methods are distinguished. Frequency-only QCM is excluded. Optional adsorption/assembly monitoring on a compatible sensor. QCM-D frequency/dissipation response is not an unqualified particle mass or an electrochemical-cell substitute.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M98">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=97"/>
    <skos:notation>M98</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>X-ray fluorescence spectrometers</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>Bulk, handheld or micro-XRF elemental analysis with element range and calibration specific to configuration. TRACER III cannot quantify carbon; trace-metal screening does not identify nanoparticle size. Optional bulk metal composition screening with suitable elemental range/calibration. Does not measure carbon content on TRACER III or nanoparticle size.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M99">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentCategory"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/categories.csv#row=98"/>
    <skos:notation>M99</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel>X-ray microscopy and tomography</skos:prefLabel>
    <icon:associationBasis>X-ray micro/nano-CT and 3D X-ray microscopy. Spatial resolution differs from voxel size; only features resolvable for the model, sample and contrast can be interpreted. Optional 3D inspection of resolvable pores/cracks in bulk nanostructured parts. Voxel size is not spatial resolution; individual nanoparticles may be unresolved.</icon:associationBasis>
  </skos:Concept>
