    <icon:claim>Theris identifies Theris TAS30 in its official product documentation.</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>curator_reviewed_catalog</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>UHV RF atom-source components for atomic species deposition/cleaning; not turnkey vacuum systems. Manufacturer product claims only. P/N links express curator relevance, not source-article apparatus, measured performance, exact host compatibility or mandatory process steps. TAS atom brochure pages 2 and 4 identify the 30 mm aperture variant. Neutral-atom source for a compatible host, distinct from the ion-source series. P19 relevance is specifically an optional nitride-PLD configuration; not apparatus from the cited P19 experiment. P46 relevance does not establish a replacement for UCLA installed hardware. Manufacturer operating envelopes are not recipe setpoints. Public purchase price and exact-model operating manual were not published in this bounded review. No documented successor relationship or newest-generation claim. No make/model match in the user-designated Purdue list; generic PVD wording is not asset identity.</icon:scope>
  </icon:SourceEvidence>
