  <icon:SourceEvidence rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence/TC-P01">
    <dct:identifier>TC-P01</dct:identifier>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv#row=982"/>
    <dct:source>
      <prov:Entity rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/TC-P01%3A1">
        <dct:title>Ontology Position List draft</dct:title>
        <icon:checkedDate>2026-10-16</icon:checkedDate>
        <icon:sourceLocator>Model boundary</icon:sourceLocator>
      </prov:Entity>
    </dct:source>
    <icon:claim>Two lid positions are a local planning abstraction. Intermediate and unknown readings, operational guards, recipes, temperatures, timing, concurrency and error recovery remain outside this draft.</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>model_assumption</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>Model-bound control documentation; not a validation of a user sequence.</icon:scope>
  </icon:SourceEvidence>
  <icon:SourceEvidence rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence/TC-P02">
    <dct:identifier>TC-P02</dct:identifier>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv#row=983"/>
    <dct:source>
      <prov:Entity rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/TC-P02%3A1">
        <dct:title>Ontology Position List draft</dct:title>
        <icon:checkedDate>2026-10-16</icon:checkedDate>
        <icon:sourceLocator>Direction admission scope</icon:sourceLocator>
      </prov:Entity>
    </dct:source>
    <icon:claim>This draft lists selected interface directions per position. It neither exhaustively admits hardware commands nor authorizes execution.</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>model_assumption</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>Model-bound control documentation; not a validation of a user sequence.</icon:scope>
  </icon:SourceEvidence>
  <icon:SourceEvidence rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence/TC-P03">
    <dct:identifier>TC-P03</dct:identifier>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv#row=984"/>
    <dct:source>
      <prov:Entity rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/TC-P03%3A1">
        <dct:title>Model-bound action interface extension</dct:title>
        <icon:checkedDate>2026-11-07</icon:checkedDate>
        <icon:sourceLocator>Thermocycler planning crosswalk v1</icon:sourceLocator>
      </prov:Entity>
    </dct:source>
    <icon:claim>The interface retains two reported lid modes for planning. Close/open directions map successful observed lid positions to those modes. The selected lid-temperature action is placed in the closed-lid mode as a local planning choice, not a manufacturer restriction. Starting conditions and completion checks are declarations; no sensor checks or execution occur here.</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>model_assumption</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>Model-bound control documentation; not a validation of a user sequence.</icon:scope>
  </icon:SourceEvidence>
